00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Good morning, John!

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.500
Let's have this conversation. I feel like

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.440
I've recently decided I just

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.280
wanna have lots of really tough

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.520
conversations on VlogBrothers. Let's, let's take these...

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.160
let's face it head on! John, I have a problem. And its name

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.160
is meat. Let's get this out of the way, there's definitely

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.440
some conflict going on between, uh, the vegetarians,

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.440
vegans of the world, and the rest

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.440
of the world. I'm gonna talk about why I think that is in this

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.440
video and I'm gonna start with the fact that vegetarians

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.440
are....right. Yes,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.440
animals raised for food do not have nice

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.440
lives and even if they did they would still

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.440
be killed in the prime of their lives so that

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.440
I could have a tasty snack. Yes, the amount of

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.440
food eaten by animals who will

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.440
later be eaten is massive. And so as

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.440
more people eat meat, more land has to be put

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.440
under cultivation. Yes, livestock contribute

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.440
massively to climate change and are a primary

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.440
reason for deforestation. And, yes, most

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.440
people don't need to eat meat to be healthy.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.440
And there are reasons both ways, like more than a

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.440
billion people make at least some of

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.440
their living from livestock. You don't wanna

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.440
take all of those peoples' livelihoods away all at once.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.440
But as the global population grows as the

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.440
global economy grows, it is very difficult

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.440
to argue that vegetarianism is not

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.440
a good thing. Basically, the important

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.440
thing here is vegetarianism allows more

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.440
people to have more food with less impact.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.440
It's good. And so, when someone

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.440
tells me that I should be a vegetarian or leaves a

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.440
comment on a video asking me how do I

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.440
justify eating meat, I have no

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.440
recourse but to say that they are right and that

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.440
I am wrong, but that I will continue

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.440
eating meat because I'm the kind

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.440
of person who has a hard time controlling

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.440
myself, and it's hard

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.440
enough not to eat a half a bag of

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.440
Oreos for breakfast. Now my personal willpower

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.440
aside, there's a fundamental conflict going on here.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.440
I live in a society where eating meat is normal

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.440
and being a vegetarian is not. It's Montana,

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.440
you guys, like, there are places in America

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.440
where vegetarianism is very normal; this is

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.440
not one of them. But there's a difference between acting in accordance

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.440
with society's expectations, which will

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.440
very rarely get you criticised

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.440
and is definitely the easy thing to do,

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.440
and actually living in a way that is

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.440
best for the future

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.440
and for people and for all of the

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.440
organisms on the planet. And that's the reality

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.440
of meat-eating. It is a thing that I don't

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.440
need to do, but I do,

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.440
despite the fact that it makes the world worse

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.440
for current animals and future

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.440
people. This is a big one for our society,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.440
but there are lots of examples of this, like

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.440
I've always found it a little bit immoral

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.440
that I spend money on things

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.440
that are not necessary like Coca-

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.440
Cola, and flying to San Francisco,

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.440
and that fifth ticket to The Force

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.440
Awakens, when there are people dying of

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.440
preventable diseases. I do those things

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.440
instead of giving that money to Save the Children for the

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.440
same reasons that I eat meat:  because it's easier,

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.440
it's simpler, I like them,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.440
and I'm not perfect. But it's also more than that,

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.440
like, acting in accordance with

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.440
society, to a certain extent,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.440
isn't just the easy thing to do,

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.440
it's also, kinda, the only

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.440
thing to do. I've experienced this, you can only

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.440
do so much breaking with culture

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.440
before you become extremely

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.440
uncomfortable. It's very hard to

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.440
find self-worth, it's very hard

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.440
to find connection... Like imagine

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.440
if every time I saw someone buy a

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.440
Coca-Cola, I, like, mumbled under my breath,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.440
like, "You know, there are people dying of preventable

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.440
diseases." I would not have a lot of friends.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.440
So why are people annoyed by vegetarians? Because

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.440
they have the audacity to work extremely

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.440
hard to live in accordance with their values.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.440
And because those values conflict

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.440
with the values of society at

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.440
large. People don't want to be told that the way that they live

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.440
their lives and the things that they enjoy

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.440
are making the world less good; especially

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.440
when you got other stuff

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.440
to worry about. But look, as frustrating

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.440
as I'm sure both sides can

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.440
find this at times, this cultural conflict is

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.440
not a bad thing. I honestly believe that we're on our

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.440
way to a better, brighter future, and 200 years

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.440
from now, people will think it's

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.440
ridiculous that we ate meat

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.440
the way that we do. There's no reason not to

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.440
appreciate vegetarians for working very

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.440
hard to live in accordance with their values, and I

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.440
completely understand their desire to convert

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.440
me and other people to their cause, to

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.440
have us eat less or no meat,

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.440
so I am thankful for you, all of you people

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.440
who tell me to not eat meat. And, yet,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.440
I am going to continue eating

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.440
less, but not no meat,

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.440
because it's easier,

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.440
it's simple, I like it,

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.440
and I'm not perfect. John,

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.440
I'll see you on Tuesday.

